+// 5650, 2 5551, 3 4444). The PSP blends, dithers and keeps the format's bits
+// in that order, so with kShaderBlend the shader blends with the GE's factors
+// and equation on the target's colour (the pass's input attachment) and the
+// pipeline does not blend. kDither adds the matrix's offset: DITH0 and DITH1
+// in kDitherRows01, DITH2 and DITH3 in kDitherRows23, 16 bits each. A PSP
+// pixel is kPixelScaleX by kPixelScaleY of the target's pixels.
